{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You shall not muzzle the ox while it threshes.</b> Like (Leviticus 10:9) ״בבאכם אל אהל מועד״ — the intent is not the actual entry, but that he not drink beforehand, so that there be no drunkenness at the time of the service; so too here, ״בדישו״ means before its threshing, so that there be no muzzling at the time of threshing; and even if he muzzled it from the outside he is liable; and so the Rabbis, blessed be their memory, stated there in Bava Metzia."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:55.907682621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}